**Session in the context.** `packages/api/src/auth.ts` builds its own `auth` with `createAuth()` and no framework cookie plugin, because the cookie plugin belongs to each app and the package cannot import an app instance. `createTRPCContext({ headers })` only calls `auth.api.getSession({ headers })` on it. Keep it read-only unless you add the app's cookie plugin to it (`createAuth(nextCookies())`, as a blueprint whose procedures change sessions does): never call endpoints that set cookies (sign-in, sign-up, sign-out, password change with `revokeOtherSessions`, ...) through this instance, because their `Set-Cookie` headers would be lost. Do those from the app's own `auth`. The factory disables session refresh on a cookie-less instance, so a tRPC read never extends a session (the refreshed cookie could not reach the browser); the app's own `auth` extends it, through `/api/auth/get-session` and server code.
